                        




A sub-infohazardous data representation implying a possible Big Rip



Item #:  SCP-5923

Containment Class: : Keter

Special Containment Procedures: 

SCP-5923 is not an Object but a Threat, it is universal in scope, it cannot be contained in any strict sense of the term. Only exposure to can be contained. The memetic contagion vector for SCP-5923 is light radiation from the early universe.

A global network of liaisons across the world’s top physics journals will screen for any papers covering the Big Rip theory and blacklist any that approach it from a correct angle. Papers promoting alternative variations such as “Quintessence”, ”Quasi Rip”, ”Little Rip” and so on must be encouraged via our partnerships with national laboratories recruitment programs and similar relationships inside academia. Under no circumstances are any public sector or academic liaisons to be told what SCP-5923 is, or even alluding to its nature in a way that may inspire curiosity; which will result in class-C amnestics administration for civilian parties and termination of any Foundation personnel responsible.

All parties worldwide discussing or posting about The Big Rip are to be put under perpetual surveillance, and targeted by advertisement to get them well-read on dead-end alternative theories so as to exhaust their curiosity on the subject. These persons of interest are then followed indefinitely to ensure their continued compliance. Foundation Class C personnel in the Memetics department produce freelance material for popular science websites promoting these theories.

All data incoming from the major scientific satellital telescopes must be filtered and all scientific professionals viewing the resulting data must be monitored. Should anyone manage to reconstruct an adequate data-footprint using simulations, or otherwise bypass our censorship, our surveillance may indicate they are witnessing info-hazardous data, the individual is to be designated SCP 5923-A and Protocol:Cataract is to be engaged. A raid team will be deployed from the nearest Foundation site to interrupt the viewing, though response times may vary such that the target would be home at the time of the raid. The target is to be shot with a tranquilizer, any persons in the domicile are to be also shot with tranquilizers, or otherwise subdued. All materials relating to SCP 5923-A’s research are to be seized.

The target is to be given a Class-A amnestic, any bystanders are to be given Class-B amnestics. If the bystanders were family members or roommates of the target, the following day a Foundation Agent posing as a friend will bring the family a gift basket and offer their heartfelt condolences for the 4th anniversary of the target’s death abroad.

Historical materials relating to a trip to a foreign country where a death certificate is easy to forge are to be introduced to the target’s computer during the raid operation, in the form of .pdf files with altered download timestamps indicating fabricated plane tickets, hotel bookings, hinging on a conference that did historically occur in that country between three and four years ago. The gift basket contains chocolates *and* a case of La Croix, both laced with class C amnestics to make the Foundation Agent be forgotten. We have found that related parties will eat the chocolates 68.5% of the time, and either the chocolates and/or the La Croix in 86.5% of cases.

It has been concluded safer to not try to re-engage the related parties in the minority case where follow-up amestics are not consumed. A death certificate is provided whenever investigated and is, essentially, a line item expense that produces legally authentic documents. Should the world change politically such that the preceding sentence is no longer true, the protocol must be adapted.

SCP-5923A becomes non-anomalous after the application of the class A amnestic. The complete personality rewrite necessitates that the Foundation pipeline the subject, now to be known as POI-5923-x, where x is the next available integer depending on how many are in the pipeline at the given time. A randomly generated number determines the new career for the confused individual, a training and re-education program is followed, and they proceed to live fairly stable lives. It was decided by the Ethics Committee not to re-introduce these persons to a career in astronomy or physics, because of the extreme threat level posed by SCP-5923 and its potential to unleash a VK-Universe Failure event.

On review of seized research materials, researchers must try to ascertain which was the last measurement taken, for our tracking purposes. This scanning exercise is done by a memetically-trained Class B operating under a Class O amnestic IV drip, with a henna tattoo of their instructions on both forearms, while wearing sunglasses. If they recognize a number they believe corresponds with the last recorded negative-pressure ratio, they must shout it out and glance away as fast as possible.



Non-infohazardous examples of quasar redshift that suggested the Big Rip theory.



Description: 

SCP-5923 is the catalyzation effect of hastening the arrival of The Big Rip by viewing a time series of measurements of distant quasar redshift, making projections from them, and tracking a progressive increase in the negative pressure ratio of the dark energy in the universe. By tracking these measurements consciously, the investigating scientist creates an observer effect that intensifies the dark energy in the universe and expedites the t-0 moment where our universe ends.

There is some debate on whether to classify the scenario as a Reality Failure or just a localized universal annihilation - while many other universes may survive. If, for example, a large number of scientists became SCP-5923-A and simultaneously tracked the negative pressure density higher, they would create a feedback loop, seeing their measurements go higher not just by their own observer effect, but by that of many. Each observer’s tick would add to the time series tracked by the next observer, creating an accelerative effect up to an asymptote. This could, for example, bring the estimated date of the Big Rip from 10^22 years in the future, to being a few years away.

Momentum: a default, naive physics imagination one might have about galaxies moving apart because of inertia from the “Big Bang”.

Momentum-prime, Acceleration: the red shifting of distant galaxies due to a baseline, steady acceleration due to a “cosmological constant” negative pressure ratio of -1. This elegant integer gives us a steadily expanding universe that ends in a long, dark, cold whimper.

Acceleration Prime, Jerk: if the red-shift of distant quasars is *stronger* than what is observed from type 1a supernovae, this may suggest the universe has a negative pressure ratio of -1, for example, -1.0012. That value would produce a Big Rip eventually, from the slow compounding not *just* of the constant dark energy in an expanding amount of space, but also, of the amount of dark energy per unit of space.

Jerk Prime, Snap: if a SCP-5923-A instance is engaged with SCP-5923, it can increase the absolute value of the negative pressure ratio from e.g. -1.0012 to -1.0013. If the SCP-5923-A instance continues to engage with SCP-5923 over subsequent sessions, the increase in the acceleration of the acceleration of spacetime will proceed steadily.

Snap Prime, Crackle: if a large number of SCP-5923-A instances were triggering more curiosity in the others, making the value go from -1.0013 to -1.01 to -1.1 to -2, and beyond, then one can project a rapid onset of pre-Big Rip effects.

Currently, after __ instances of SCP-5923-A the negative pressure ratio has shifted to -1.__, which presently leaves us with many billions of years. The earlier estimate of a Big Rip date in the very far future, when the theory was young and SCP-5923 was yet undetected, is unfortunately now a foregone reality.

Big Rip effects:

Phase 1 : Isolation of Galaxy Cluster in the Void; all external light red shifts to black

This is normally expected to take hundreds of billions of years, many doubling periods of 7 billion years, under a -1 energy pressure ratio, but will dawn much faster now. Current worst-case scenario projections consider this phase reachable in a minimum time of one-week of large-scale SCP-5923-A activity.

Phase 2 : Pulling of Galaxy Cluster

Assuming Andromeda and the Milky Way have not yet fused by the onset of phase 2, such as in a Situation: Crackle or Situation: Snap, then the galaxies would slowly glide apart, then faster. Crackle projects 3.5 days after Phase 1.

Phase 3 : Andromeda Red-shifts into the Night

Another 2 days, worst-case.

Phase 4 : Milky Way stars red-shift

We’d see this phenomenon first with the more distant stars, with the light reaching us from the galactic core being-blue shifted, the blue sub-phase would last about 4 or 6 hours in a Crackle. The Foundation would probably activate SCP-xxxx and send everyone home to be able to enjoy it. We wouldn’t see the spreading of the stars in our galaxy or its spiral shape being kneaded into a more globular elliptical, because there would not be nearly enough time for that light to reach us.

Phase 5 : Separation of The Solar System

Worst-case, this takes about 90 to 100 minutes. Because we are 8 light-minutes away from the sun, we would not see the already orange-spectrum sunlight start to significantly red shift until we had reached an orbital distance of 10 AU. In the last 10 or 20 minutes of this period the earth’s orbit would find its path out where the Oort cloud used to be. Those who have adequate shelter and energy would probably survive the first half of this period but atmospheric disturbances would begin depriving non-Foundation populations of oxygen.

Phase 6 : Tidal Shearing of The Earth

Worst-case estimate, 25 minutes.

Phase 7 : Bunker Rupture

10 minutes.

Phase 8 : Holding On To Someone While Dying in The Vacuum

3-4 minutes.

Phase 9 : SCPs, O5 and below personnel with adequate gear, other GoI personnel with adequate gear, the last surviving entities, begin to be torn apart due to the repulsive phantom energy overcoming electromagnetic chemical bonds.

90 seconds

Phase 10 : SCP-2100-4 begins to shear apart.

Phase 11 : All spacetime anomaly SCPs begin to have scalar manifold interactions with the dark energy singularity in unpredictable ways. All spatially infinite structural anomalies are unfurled, releasing energy into the void. SCP-2821 may have already become unstable far sooner and achieved the same effect. The phase-transition bubble may end up being the only place in the universe where structural physics can persist.

Phase 12 : The complete rupturing of the fabric of non-anomalous spacetime.

Phase 13 : Possible ekpyrotic universal creation event involving interaction between SCP-179, which we believe would still be alive based on the suggestion of [redacted] first encountered in the [redacted] in 1932.

Addendum: 

The below image has been expunged of any traces of SCP-5923-1, it is believed that SCP-5923-1 has info-hazardous properties that lead those who see it to become an instance of SCP-5923-A.



SCP-5923-1



If we had not expunged the details from the center of the image, you would see in approximately the central pixels, in the white space of the central quasar’s shine, two slight discolorations that appear to be eyes, surrounded by a smooth, slightly oval contour of discoloration that appears to define the boundary of a small head, with appearance similar to classical grey aliens. This impression, SCP-5923-1, is something we detected in the recovered materials of at least 56% of SCP-5923-A subjects. This overlaid face is not found in the original satellite imaging of these quasars, by expunging it from the above image we are returning the quasar scan to its original, non-anomalous state.

It is believed that staring into SCP-5923-1 increases the risk that a subject may become an instance of SCP-5923-A. It has been speculated, but we are unable to test, that the amount of time a subject spends staring into an un-expunged SCP-5923-1 image amplifies the impact they will have on worsening negative pressure ratios by engaging with SCP-5923.







                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
